From: gts7l project
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: freeze user invokes in place instead of
 interrupting them

fastrpc_internal_invoke() waits for a user invoke with
wait_for_completion_interruptible(). A system suspend freezes user space
by sending each task a fake signal, which ends the wait with -ERESTARTSYS
after the message has already been sent to the DSP. The context is kept,
and the syscall is then restarted automatically on thaw, sending the same
invoke to the DSP a second time with a new context.

For a reverse-RPC listener (hexagonrpcd's adsp_listener next2 call),
that message carries the reply to the DSP's previous request, so the DSP
receives the same reply twice. On the Galaxy Tab S7 (SM8250) the SLPI's
sensor_process dies of it at every resume, and even on a freezer-only
pm_test ("PDM: service 'sensor_process' crash: EX:sensor_process:0x1:
frpc_dsp:0x75"). remoteproc then restarts the SLPI and every sensor
client loses its connection.

Wait with TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE instead. The freezer then
parks the task in the wait (TASK_FROZEN) without a signal, so the
syscall is neither interrupted nor restarted. A reply that arrives
meanwhile is kept as an expected wakeup and seen on thaw. A real signal
still interrupts the wait as before.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index eb6c2a78d..5c4913b18 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1278,7 +1278,16 @@ static int fastrpc_internal_invoke(struct fastrpc_user *fl,  u32 kernel,
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		/*
+		 * Freezable: the freezer parks the task here instead of
+		 * interrupting the wait. An interrupted invoke returns
+		 * -ERESTARTSYS and the syscall restart sends the same message
+		 * to the DSP again; for a reverse-RPC listener that repeats the
+		 * previous reply, which kills the DSP-side process (SLPI
+		 * sensor_process: "frpc_dsp" fatal error at every resume).
+		 */
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+						TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	if (err)
